{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-7790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-5{y}^{′}-14y=0,\\,y(1)=2,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(1)=5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-5\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}-14{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda -14) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda -14 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -7)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =-2$ or $\\lambda =7.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{7x}.\n$$\n\nNow let us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(1)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA{e}^{-2}+B{e}^{7}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=5.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-2A{e}^{-2x}+7B{e}^{7x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-2A{e}^{-2}+7B{e}^{7}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{-2}+B{e}^{7}=2 \\\\ -2A{e}^{-2}+7B{e}^{7}=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A={e}^{2},B={e}^{-7}.$\n\nNow we get the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{-2x}+{e}^{-7}\\cdot {e}^{7x} \\\\ y & ={e}^{-2x+2}+{e}^{7x-7}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-7790" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7790" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=4{e}^{-2x+2}-2{e}^{7x-7}"] ["math" "y=4{e}^{-3x}-2{e}^{4x}"] ["math" "y=5{e}^{-2x+2}-3{e}^{7x-7}"] ["math" "y={e}^{-2x+2}+{e}^{7x-7}"] ["math" "y={e}^{3x-3}+{e}^{4x-4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7790" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={e}^{-2x+2}+{e}^{7x-7}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+10y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{-2x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+10y=0,\\,y(0)=-3,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-3$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=-3.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-3,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-5A{e}^{-5x}-2B{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-3$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-5A-2B=-3.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=-3 \\\\ -5A-2B=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=3,B=-6.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=3{e}^{-5x}-6{e}^{-2x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-94011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-5{e}^{-5x}+2{e}^{-2x}"] ["math" "y=-{e}^{-5x}-2{e}^{-2x}"] ["math" "y=2{e}^{-5x}-5{e}^{-2x}"] ["math" "y=3{e}^{-5x}-6{e}^{-2x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{-5x}-4{e}^{-2x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=3{e}^{-5x}-6{e}^{-2x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+12y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{-4x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+12y=0,\\,y(0)=-3,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-3$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=-3.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3A{e}^{-3x}-4B{e}^{-4x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-3A-4B=2.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=-3 \\\\ -3A-4B=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=-10,B=7.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-10{e}^{-3x}+7{e}^{-4x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-7788" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7788" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-10{e}^{-3x}+7{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "y=-12{e}^{-3x}+9{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "y=-9{e}^{-3x}+6{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "y=3{e}^{-3x}-6{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "y=7{e}^{-3x}-10{e}^{-4x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7788" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-10{e}^{-3x}+7{e}^{-4x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-6{y}^{′}+8y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{4x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-6{y}^{′}+8y=0,\\,y(0)=9,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=24.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=9$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=9.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=24,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2A{e}^{2x}+4B{e}^{4x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=24$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A+4B & =24 \\\\ A+2B & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=9 \\\\ A+2B=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=6,B=3.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6{e}^{2x}+3{e}^{4x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-94007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=2{e}^{2x}+7{e}^{4x}"] ["math" "y=5{e}^{2x}+4{e}^{4x}"] ["math" "y=6{e}^{2x}+3{e}^{4x}"] ["math" "y=8{e}^{2x}+{e}^{4x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{2x}+8{e}^{4x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=6{e}^{2x}+3{e}^{4x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-8{y}^{′}+15y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +15 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -5) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =3,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{3x}+B{e}^{5x}.\n$$\n\nNow we find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=2.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3A{e}^{3x}+5B{e}^{5x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n3A+5B=2.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=2 \\\\ 3A+5B=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=4,B=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4{e}^{3x}-2{e}^{5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-94006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-2{e}^{3x}+4{e}^{5x}"] ["math" "y=-4{e}^{3x}+6{e}^{5x}"] ["math" "y=3{e}^{3x}-{e}^{5x}"] ["math" "y=4{e}^{3x}-2{e}^{5x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{3x}+{e}^{5x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=4{e}^{3x}-2{e}^{5x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+16y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-4x}+Bx{e}^{-4x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+16y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=1.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-4A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{-4x}-4Bx{e}^{-4x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-4A+B=-2.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=1$ gives $B=2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-4x}+2x{e}^{-4x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-130348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y={e}^{-4x}+2x{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{-4x}+x{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{-4x}-2x{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{-4x}-3x{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{-4x}-x{e}^{-4x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={e}^{-4x}+2x{e}^{-4x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-65116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the functions  ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{4x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=x{e}^{4x}$ are solutions to the equation ${y}^{″}-8{y}^{′}+16y=0,$ solve the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-8{y}^{′}+16y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-65116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "According to the superposition principle, any linear combination of the functions  ${y}_{1}(x)$  and ${y}_{2}(x)$  must be a solution to the original differential equation.\n\nHence, the general solution is: \n\n$$\ny={c}_{1}{e}^{4x}+{c}_{2}x{e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nNow, we find constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-1.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=(4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}){e}^{4x}+4{c}_{2}x{e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${y}^{′}(0)=-1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1=4(1)+{c}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{4x}-5x{e}^{4x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-65116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-65116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-65116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y={e}^{4x}+2x{e}^{4x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{4x}+4x{e}^{4x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{4x}-5x{e}^{4x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{4x}-6x{e}^{4x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{4x}-x{e}^{4x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-65116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={e}^{4x}-5x{e}^{4x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-8{y}^{′}+16y=0,\\,y(1)=2,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(1)=-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-8\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+16{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +16) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +16 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -4) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =4$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{4x}+Bx{e}^{4x}.\n$$\n\nLet us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(1)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA{e}^{4}+B{e}^{4}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=-1.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4A{e}^{4x}+B{e}^{4x}+4Bx{e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n4A{e}^{4}+5B{e}^{4}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{4}+B{e}^{4}=2 \\\\ 4A{e}^{4}+5B{e}^{4}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=11{e}^{-4},B=-9{e}^{-4}.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =11{e}^{-4}\\cdot {e}^{4x}-9{e}^{-4}\\cdot x{e}^{4x} \\\\  & =11{e}^{4x-4}-9x{e}^{4x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-7798" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7798" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-7{e}^{4x-4}+9x{e}^{4x-4}"] ["math" "y=11{e}^{4x-4}-9x{e}^{4x-4}"] ["math" "y=3{e}^{2x-2}-x{e}^{2x-2}"] ["math" "y=5{e}^{4x-4}-3x{e}^{4x-4}"] ["math" "y=8{e}^{2x-2}-6x{e}^{2x-2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7798" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=11{e}^{4x-4}-9x{e}^{4x-4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+20{y}^{′}+100y=0,\\,y(0)=5,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+20\\lambda +100 & =0 \\\\ {(\\lambda +10)}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have a repeated root $\\lambda =-10,$ so we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-10x}+Bx{e}^{-10x}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=5$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=5.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-5,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-10A{e}^{-10x}+B{e}^{-10x}-10Bx{e}^{-10x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-5$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-10A+B=-5.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=5$ gives $B=45.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=5{e}^{-10x}+45x{e}^{-10x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-130345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-5{e}^{10x}+x{e}^{10x}"] ["math" "y=5{e}^{-10x}+27x{e}^{-10x}"] ["math" "y=5{e}^{-10x}+45x{e}^{-10x}"] ["math" "y=5{e}^{-10x}+x{e}^{-10x}"] ["math" "y=5{e}^{10x}+2{e}^{-10x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=5{e}^{-10x}+45x{e}^{-10x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+\\frac{9y}{4}=0,\\,y(1)={e}^{-1/2},\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(1)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-1/2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+3\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+\\frac{9}{4}{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +\\frac{9}{4}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +\\frac{9}{4} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +\\frac{3}{2})(\\lambda +\\frac{3}{2}) & =0 \\\\ {(\\lambda +\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =\\frac{3}{2}$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x/2}+Bx{e}^{-3x/2}.\n$$\n\nLet us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \nSubstituting $y(1)={e}^{-1/2}$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{-3/2}+B{e}^{-3/2} & ={e}^{-1/2} \\\\ A+B & =e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-1/2}.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\frac{3}{2}A{e}^{-3/2x}+B{e}^{-3/2x}-\\frac{3}{2}Bx{e}^{-3/2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-1/2}$ into the above gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}A{e}^{-3/2}-\\frac{1}{2}B{e}^{-3/2} & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-1/2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}A-\\frac{1}{2}B & =\\frac{1}{2}e \\\\ -3A-B & =e\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=e \\\\ -3A-B=e\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=-e,B=2e.$\n\nNow we get the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-e\\cdot {e}^{-3x/2}+2e\\cdot x{e}^{-3x/2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-3x/2+1}+2x{e}^{-3x/2+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-7815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-2{e}^{x/2-1}+3x{e}^{x/2-1}"] ["math" "y=-{e}^{-3x/2+1}+2x{e}^{-3x/2+1}"] ["math" "y=-{e}^{x/2-1}+2x{e}^{x/2-1}"] ["math" "y=3{e}^{-3x/2+1}-2x{e}^{-3x/2+1}"] ["math" "y=x{e}^{-3x/2+1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7815" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-{e}^{-3x/2+1}+2x{e}^{-3x/2+1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+64y=0,\\,y(\\pi )=1,\\,{y}^{′}(\\pi )=4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+64 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-64 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 8\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =P\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(\\pi )=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(\\pi )=4,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-8P\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+8Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(\\pi )=4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8Q=4\\,⟹\\,Q=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-94023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+49y=0,\\,y(\\pi )=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(\\pi )=7.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+49 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-49 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 7\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =P\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(\\pi )=-2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-P=-2\\,⟹\\,P=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(\\pi )=7,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-7P\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x+7Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(\\pi )=7$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7Q=7\\,⟹\\,Q=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-94022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x"] ["math" "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x"] ["math" "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x"] ["math" "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x"] ["math" "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡7x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡7x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+100y=0,\\,y(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=10,\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=50.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+100 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-100 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 10\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =P\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=10$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=50,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-10P\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x+10Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=50$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10P=50\\,⟹\\,P=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-130355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x"] ["math" "y=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x"] ["math" "y=10\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x"] ["math" "y=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+144y=0,\\,y(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=1,\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=24.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+144 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-144 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 12\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =P\\operatorname{cos}⁡12x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-Q=1\\,⟹\\,Q=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=24,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-12P\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x+12Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡12x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=24$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12P=24\\,⟹\\,P=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡12x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-130356" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130356" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡12x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x"] ["math" "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x"] ["math" "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡12x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x"] ["math" "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡12x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130356" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡12x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡12x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2y=0,\\,y(0)=-4,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=4\\sqrt{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-2 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =P\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-4$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=4\\sqrt{2},$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\sqrt{2}P\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+\\sqrt{2}Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=4\\sqrt{2}$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2}Q=4\\sqrt{2}\\,⟹\\,Q=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-94020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)"] ["math" "y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)"] ["math" "y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)"] ["math" "y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)"] ["math" "y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)-4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-94020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+8y=0,\\,y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={e}^{\\pi },\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=4{e}^{\\pi }.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4)-4+8 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ \\lambda -2 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =2\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={e}^{\\pi }$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-P{e}^{\\pi } & ={e}^{\\pi } \\\\ P & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=4{e}^{\\pi },$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2{e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+{e}^{2x}(-2P\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=4{e}^{\\pi }$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2P{e}^{\\pi }-2Q{e}^{\\pi } & =4{e}^{\\pi } \\\\ -2P-2Q & =4 \\\\ 2-2Q & =4 \\\\ Q & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $P=-1$ and $Q=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{2x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) \\\\  & =-{e}^{2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c4e29dd259a0b73c75efb40cbcc43d96a86a409fde5103019e0c01c90e2bf14"} {"question" "q-7892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-{e}^{2x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)"] ["math" "y=-{e}^{2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)"] ["math" "y=-{e}^{2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)"] ["math" "y={e}^{2x}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)"] ["math" "y={e}^{2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-7892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-{e}^{2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+26y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+26y=0,\\,y(0)=-4,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f7c5babf314148d41fcf25ca864e6228b45ac387d5e81d0c4"} {"question" "q-130371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-4$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=-4.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=1,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={e}^{x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x)+{e}^{x}(-5P\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+5Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x).\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=1$ into the above to get\n\n$$\nP+5Q=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $P=-4$ gives $Q=1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064694/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca21b24c36ae88f